@startuml
!theme cyborg
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F4F6
skinparam ArrowColor #CBD5E1
allowmixing
title Proposed — Candidate tactics mapped to scenario responsibilities
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

package "Trusted modular application responsibilities" {
 component "Owner operation\ncurrent authority + expected versions" as A
 component "Guarded local persistence\ncoherent state / identity / reference protection" as D
 component "Bounded admission / worker lanes\nheadroom + actual progress observation" as W
 component "Scoped derived cache\nexact inputs + current eligibility" as C
 component "Adapter / durable attempt\nactual partial/unknown observations" as E
 A --> D : integrity / change isolation
 A --> C : measured processing benefit only if correct
 A --> W : bounded resource demand
 W --> E : eligible attributable dispatch
}
rectangle "Separate enabling evidence\nUntrusted execution containment" as I
rectangle "Independent usable recovery set\nrecords / bytes / repositories / keys / current authority" as R
W ..> I : prerequisite, not selected product
D ..> R : consistent recoverability required
note bottom of R
 Modularity supports change boundaries but is not proof of modifiability.
 Cache, queues and recovery drawings do not establish installed facilities.
 Actual scenario evidence must assess benefits and adverse effects.
end note

@enduml